ot\in B(\mathbf{a}^*,\epsilon) \,\middle|\, { oldsymbol \alpha}^{(0)}\in B(\mathbf{a}^*,\epsilon)ight] \leq T\exp(-\Omega(\epsilon^2 n)) \end{align*} and thus, the stopping time $	au$ satisfies $	au\geq\exp(\Omega(\epsilon^2 n))$ w.h.p.~if $\epsilon = \omega(\max\{\sqrt{\log n/n}, \sqrt{1/np}\})$.

In this section, we prove \cref{prop:escape}. Let $\mathbf{a}^*$ be a fixed point satisfying \cref{asm:escape_assumption0}. The proof of \cref{prop:escape} consists of two parts: We derive \cref{prop:escape} from \cref{asm:escape_assumption1,asm:escape_assumption2}. Recall the random variable ${ oldsymbol  eta}$ defined in \cref{eqn:betadef}. From the definition \cref{eqn:betadef}, each element $ eta_i$ of ${ oldsymbol  eta}$ can be rewritten as  egin{align}  eta_i&=\sum_{j=1}^2 u_{ij} \alpha_j-(U\mathbf{a}^*)_i, \end{align} where we let $U=(u_{ij})$. Each element $u_{ij}$ of the matrix $U$ does not depend on $n$. Hence, the Hoeffding bound (\cref{lem:Hoeffding}) implies  egin{align} \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}[| eta'_i-\mathbf{E}[ eta'_i]|\geq t]\leq \exp\left(-\Omega(t^2n)ight). \end{align} From \cref{thm:approximation_vectorfield} and the Taylor expansion \cref{eqn:Taylorexpansion}, we have  egin{align*} \mathbf{E}[{ oldsymbol  eta}' \mid A] &= \mathbf{E}[U({ oldsymbol \alpha}'-\mathbf{a}^*) \mid A]\ &=U(H({ oldsymbol \alpha})-\mathbf{a}^*)+O\left( rac{1}{\sqrt{np}}ight)\cdot \mathbf{1}\ &=UJ({ oldsymbol \alpha}-\mathbf{a}^*)+\left(O_{{ oldsymbol \alpha}	o \mathbf{a}^*}(\|{ oldsymbol \alpha}-\mathbf{a}^*\|_\infty^2)+O\left( rac{1}{\sqrt{np}}ight)ight)\cdot \mathbf{1}\ &=\Lambda { oldsymbol  eta}+\left(O_{\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|	o 0}(\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty^2)+O\left( rac{1}{\sqrt{np}}ight)ight)\cdot \mathbf{1}. \end{align*} Hence, the $i$-th element $ eta_i$ of ${ oldsymbol  eta}=( eta_1\, eta_2)^{	op}$ satisfies  egin{align} |\mathbf{E}[ eta'_i]| = |\lambda_i\| eta_i|+O_{\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|	o 0}(\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty^2)+O\left( rac{1}{\sqrt{np}}ight). \end{align} It is convenient to consider the behavior of ${ oldsymbol  eta}$ instead of ${ oldsymbol \alpha}$. Note that ${ oldsymbol \alpha}	o \mathbf{a}^*$ implies ${ oldsymbol  eta}	o \mathbf{0}$ and vice versa since the matrix $U$ is nonsingular. By substituting $t=\Theta\left(\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}ight)$ to \cref{eqn:beta_concentration}, for sufficiently large constant $C>0$, it holds w.h.p.~that  egin{align} \left| | eta'_i| - |\lambda_i|| eta_i| ight| \leq C\|{ oldmath  eta}\|_{\infty}^2+ C\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}. \end{align} \paragraph*{Derive \cref{prop:escape} from \cref{asm:escape_assumption1}} Suppose that the fixed point $\mathbf{a}^*$ satisfies \cref{asm:escape_assumption1}. Let $I_{>1} \mathrel{\mathop:}= \{i\in[2]:|\lambda_i|>1\}$ and $I_{\leq 1} \mathrel{\mathop:}= [2]\setminus I_{>1}$. Fix a sufficiently large constant $K>0$ and let $\epsilon^*$ be the constant mentioned in \cref{asm:escape_assumption1}. Define  egin{align*} \mathcal{A}_1&=\left\{A\subseteq V\,:\, \|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty \leq \epsilon^* 	ext{ and }| eta_j|< K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}} 	ext{ for all }j\in I_{>1} ight\},\ \mathcal{A}_2&=\left\{A\subseteq V\,:\, \|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty \leq \epsilon^* 	ext{ and }| eta_j|\geq K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}} 	ext{ for some }j\in I_{>1} ight\},\ \mathcal{A}_3&=\left\{A\subseteq V\,:\, \|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty >\epsilon^* 	ext{ and }| eta_j|\leq \epsilon^* 	ext{ for all }j\in I_{\leq 1} ight\}. \end{align*} We claim that, for each $i=1,2$ and any $A\in \mathcal{A}_i$, there exists $	au=O(\log n)$ satisfying $\mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}\left[A^{(	au)}\in \mathcal{A}_{i+1}\,\middle| A^{(0)}=A ight] \geq 1-n^{-\Omega(1)}$. This completes the proof of \cref{prop:escape} under \cref{asm:escape_assumption1}. \paragraph*{Case I: $A^{(0)}\in \mathcal{A}_1$.} Let $f(A)\mathrel{\mathop:}= \lfloor n\max\{| eta_i|:i\in I_{>1}\}floor$ and $m=K\sqrt{n\log n}$. We use \cref{cor:nazocor} to show $A^{(	au)}\in \mathcal{A}_2$ for some $	au=O(\log n)$. Here, we use $\mathcal{A}_1$ as $\mathcal{B}$ of \cref{cor:nazocor}. Note that $A\in\mathcal{A}_1$ implies $f(A)<m$. From \cref{eqn:beta_sum_of_irv} and ef{asm:asm2}, we have $\mathop{\mathbf{Var}}[| eta_i| \mid A]=\sum_{j\in[2]} u_{ij}^2 \mathop{\mathbf{Var}}[\alpha_j \mid A]=\Omega(n^{-1})$. Here, note that, for every $i\in[2]$, there exists $j\in[2]$ such that $u_{ij}
eq 0$, since otherwise, it contradicts to the fact that the matrix $U$ is nonsingular. Thus, from \cref{cor:BEbound_cor}, it holds that, for any constant $h>0$, there exists a positive constant $C_1<1$ such that $\mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}[f(A')< h\sqrt{n} \mid f(A)\leq m] < C_1.$ This verifies the condition~ef{cond:nazo_sqrt} of \cref{cor:nazocor}. Now we check the condition~ef{cond:chernoff}. Let $z\in[2]$ be the least index satisfying $| eta_z|=\max\{| eta_i|:i\in[2]\}$. Suppose that $A\in \mathcal{A}_1$ satisfies $f(A)=\lfloor n| eta_z|floor \geq h\sqrt{n}$ for sufficiently large constant $h> rac{100 C}{\epsilon_1}$ (recall that the constant $\epsilon_1$ is mentioned in ef{asm:asm4}). Then, from ef{asm:asm4}, we have  egin{align*} |\mathbf{E}[ eta'_z \mid A]| &\geq (1+0.99\epsilon_1)| eta_z| + 0.01\epsilon_1| eta_z|- rac{C}{\sqrt{n}} \geq (1+0.99\epsilon_1)| eta_z|. \end{align*} Thus, from the Hoeffding inequality (\cref{lem:Hoeffding}), we obtain  egin{align*} \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}[f(A')<(1+0.98\epsilon_1)f(A) \mid A] \leq \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}\left[f(A')< rac{1+0.98\epsilon_1}{1+0.99\epsilon_1}\mathbf{E}[f(A')]\,\middle|\,Aight] \leq \exp\left(-\Omega\left( rac{f(A)^2}{n}ight)ight) \end{align*} holds for every $A\in \mathcal{A}_1$ satisfying $f(A)\geq h\sqrt{n}$. This verifies the condition~ef{cond:chernoff}. Finally, we check the condition~ef{cond:whp} of \cref{cor:nazocor}. From ef{asm:asm5}, it holds that  egin{align*} \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}[A'
ot\in \mathcal{A}_1	ext{ and }f(A')<m \mid A\in \mathcal{A}_1] \leq \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}[\exists j\in I_{\leq 1},| eta'_j|>\epsilon^* \mid A\in\mathcal{A}_1] \leq n^{-\Omega(1)}. \end{align*} Therefore, from \cref{cor:nazocor}, we have $f(A^{(	au)})\geq m=K\sqrt{n\log n}$ (i.e.~$A^{(	au)}\in \mathcal{A}_2$) holds w.h.p.~for some $	au=O(\log n)$. \paragraph*{Case I\hspace{-.1em}I: $A^{(0)}\in \mathcal{A}_2$.} Suppose that $A^{(0)}\in\mathcal{A}_2$ and let $j\in I_{>1}$ be the index satisfying $| eta_j|>K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}$. We remark that $K$ is sufficiently large. From ef{asm:asm4} and \cref{eqn:beta'bounds}, we have $| eta'_j|\geq (1+0.99\epsilon_1)| eta_j|$. Thus, for some $	au=O(\log n)$, we have $| eta^{(	au)}_j|>\epsilon^*$. Moreover, from ef{asm:asm5}, we have $| eta^{(	au)}_i|\leq\epsilon^*$ for all $i\in I_{\leq 1}$. Therefore, $A^{(	au)}\in \mathcal{A}_3$ holds w.h.p. \paragraph*{Derive \cref{prop:escape} from \cref{asm:escape_assumption2}} Suppose that the fixed point $\mathbf{a}^*$ satisfies \cref{asm:escape_assumption2}. Let  egin{align*} I_{<1}&\mathrel{\mathop:}=\{i\in[2]:|\lambda_i|<1\}, \ I_{>1}&\mathrel{\mathop:}=\{i\in[2]:|\lambda_i|>1\}. \end{align*} From ef{asm:asm6}, we have $I_{<1}\cup I_{>1}=[2]$. Moreover, there exists some constant $\epsilon>0$ such that  egin{align} ||\lambda_i|-1| > 3\epsilon \end{align} holds for every $i\in [2]$. For $A\subseteq V$, let $z=z(A)\in[2]$ be the least index satisfying $| eta_z|=\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty$. We use four constants: In \cref{eqn:beta'bounds,eqn:epsdef}, we defined $C$ and $\epsilon$. Let $K\mathrel{\mathop:}= rac{C}{\epsilon}$ and $\epsilon'\mathrel{\mathop:}=  rac{\epsilon}{C}$. Consider four events  egin{align*} \mathcal{B}_1&=\left\{A\subseteq V\,:\, K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}<\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty \leq \epsilon' 	ext{ and }z(A)\in I_{<1} ight\},\ \mathcal{B}_2&=\left\{A\subseteq V\,:\, \|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty \leq K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}} ight\}, \ \mathcal{B}_3&=\left\{A\subseteq V\,:\, K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}<\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty \leq \epsilon' 	ext{ and }z(A)\in I_{>1} ight\}, \ \mathcal{B}_4&=\left\{A\subseteq V\,:\, \|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty > \epsilon' 	ext{ and } | eta_j|\leq \epsilon'	ext{ for all }j\in I_{<1} ight\}. \end{align*} We claim that, if $A^{(0)}\in \mathcal{B}_i$, then $A^{(	au)}
ot \in \cup_{1\leq j\leq i}\mathcal{B}_{j}$ holds w.h.p.~for any $i\in\{1,2,3\}$ and some $	au=O(\log n)$. This completes the proof of \cref{prop:escape} under \cref{asm:escape_assumption2}. \paragraph*{Case I: $A^{(0)}\in\mathcal{B}_1$.} Suppose $A^{(0)}\in \mathcal{B}_1$. We argue that, if $A^{(t)}\in \mathcal{B}_1$, then either $A^{(t+1)}\in \mathcal{B}_3$ or $\|{ oldsymbol  eta}^{(t+1)}\|_\infty \leq (1-\epsilon)\|{ oldsymbol  eta}^{(t)}\|_\infty$ holds w.h.p. For any $j\in I_{<1}$, the bound \cref{eqn:beta'bounds} yields that  egin{align*} | eta'_j| &\leq (1-3\epsilon)\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty +C\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|^2_\infty + C\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}} \ &\leq (1-\epsilon)\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty - 2\epsilon \| eta\|_\infty + C\epsilon'\| eta\|_\infty + C\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}} \ &= (1-\epsilon)\| eta\|_\infty - \epsilon\| eta\|_\infty + C\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}} \ &\leq (1-\epsilon)\| eta\|_\infty-(\epsilon K-C)\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}} \ &\leq (1-\epsilon)\| eta\|_\infty \end{align*} holds w.h.p. If $A^{(t+1)}
ot\in\mathcal{B}_3$, then $\|{ oldsymbol  eta}'\|_\infty = | eta'_j|$ for some $j\in I_{<1}$; thus, we have $\|{ oldsymbol  eta}'\|_\infty \leq (1-\epsilon)\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty$ w.h.p. Therefore, for some $	au=O(\log n)$, either $A^{(	au)}\in \mathcal{B}_2$ or $A^{(	au)}\in \mathcal{B}_{3}$ holds w.h.p. \paragraph*{Case I\hspace{-.1em}I: $A^{(0)}\in\mathcal{B}_2$.} Suppose $A^{(0)}\in \mathcal{B}_2$. Our strategy is to apply \cref{cor:nazocor}. We will prove the following result in the last part of this subsection.  egin{lemma} Conditioned on $A\in \mathcal{B}_2$, the followings hold w.h.p.:  egin{enumerate}[label=(oman*)] \item For every $i\in I_{<1}$, it holds that $| eta'_i|\leq K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}$. \item there exists a constant $h>0$ such that, for every $i\in I_{>1}$,  egin{align*} \left|\mathbf{E}\left[ eta'_i\,\middle|\,A,| eta_i|\geq  rac{h}{\sqrt{n}}ight]ight| \geq (1+\epsilon) | eta_i|. \end{align*} \end{enumerate} \end{lemma} Let $m=K\sqrt{n\log n}$ and define $f(A)\mathrel{\mathop:}=\left\lfloor n\cdot \max_{i\in I_{>1}}| eta_i| ightfloor$. Suppose that $f(A^{(	au)}) \geq K\sqrt{n\log n} $ holds w.h.p.~for some $	au=O(\log n)$. Then, we have $A^{(	au)}
ot\in\mathcal{B}_1\cup\mathcal{B}_2$ w.h.p.~since $| eta_i^{(	au)}|\leq K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}$ holds w.h.p.~for any $i\in I_{< 1}$. Here, we used ef{state:small} of \cref{lem:beta'bounds}. To show $f(A^{(	au)}) \geq K\sqrt{n\log n}$, we check the condition ef{cond:nazo_sqrt} to ef{cond:whp} of \cref{cor:nazocor} and then apply it. First, we check the condition~ef{cond:nazo_sqrt} of \cref{cor:nazocor}. We use the same argument described in the Case I in \cref{sec:derivethm2.11fromasm2.9}. From \cref{eqn:beta_sum_of_irv}, we have $\mathop{\mathbf{Var}}[ eta'_i \mid A]\geq \sum_{j=1}^2 u_{ij}^2 \mathop{\mathbf{Var}}[\alpha'_j \mid A]$. Moreover, for every $i\in[2]$ there exists $j\in[2]$ such that $u_{ij}
eq 0$, since otherwise, it contradicts to the fact that $U$ is nonsingular. From ef{asm:asm2}, we have $\mathop{\mathbf{Var}}[ eta'_i \mid A]=\Omega(n^{-1})$; thus, from \cref{cor:BEbound_cor}, it holds that, for any constant $h>0$, there exists a positive constant $C_1<1$ such that $\mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}[f(A')\geq h\sqrt{n} \mid f(A)\leq m] < C_1$. We check the condition~ef{cond:chernoff} of \cref{cor:nazocor}. For every $i\in I_{>1}$, \cref{lem:beta'bounds} yields  egin{align} |\mathbf{E}[ eta^{(t+1)}_i \mid A^{(t)}\in\mathcal{B}_2]| \geq (1+\epsilon) | eta^{(t)}_i|. \end{align} In look at \cref{eqn:beta_sum_of_irv}, from the Hoeffding inequality (\cref{lem:Hoeffding}), it holds for any set $A^{(t)}\in\mathcal{B}_2$, any index $i\in I_{>1}$ and any constant $\epsilon'>0$ that  egin{align} \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}[| eta'_i| \leq (1-\epsilon')|\mathbf{E}[ eta_i']|]&\leq \exp\left(-\Omega\left(\epsilon'^2\mathbf{E}[ eta'_i]^2night)ight) \leq \exp\left(-\Omega\left(\epsilon'^2 rac{f(A)^2}{n}ight)ight). \end{align} From \cref{eqn:beta_expect,eqn:beta_hoeffding}, by letting $\epsilon'= rac{\epsilon}{2(1+\epsilon)}$, we obtain  egin{align*} \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}\left[| eta^{(t+1)}_i| \leq \left(1+ rac{\epsilon}{2}ight)\cdot | eta^{(t)}_i| \,\middle|\,A^{(t)}\in \mathcal{B}_2ight] &\leq \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}\left[| eta'_i| \leq (1-\epsilon') \cdot |\mathbf{E}[ eta_i' \mid A^{(t)}\in\mathcal{B}_2] |ight]\ &\leq \exp\left(-\Omega\left( rac{f(A)^2}{n}ight)ight). \end{align*} In other words, for any $A\in\mathcal{B}_2$ satisfying $f(A)\geq h\sqrt{n}$ for some constant $h>0$, we have  egin{align*} \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}\left[f(A^{(t+1)})<\left(1+ rac{\epsilon}{2}ight)f(A^{(t)})\,\middle|\,A^{(t)}=A ight]\leq \exp\left(-\Omega\left( rac{f(A)^2}{n}ight)ight). \end{align*} Finally, we check the condition~ef{cond:whp} of \cref{cor:nazocor}. From \cref{lem:beta'bounds}, we have  egin{align*} \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}[A^{(t+1)}
ot\in \mathcal{B}_2 \land f(A^{(t+1)})\leq m \mid A^{(t)}\in\mathcal{B}_2] &\leq \mathop{\mathbf{Pr}}\left[\exists j\in I_{<1}:\,| eta'_j|> K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}\,\middle|\,A\in\mathcal{B}_2ight] \ &\leq n^{-\Omega(1)}. \end{align*} Now we are ready to apply \cref{cor:nazocor}. Thus, there exists $	au=O(\log n)$ such that $f(A^{(	au)})\geq K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}$ and $| eta^{(	au)}_j| \leq K\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}$ hold w.h.p.~for every $j\in I_{<1}$. Consequently, $A^{(	au)}\in \mathcal{B}_3 \cup \mathcal{B}_4$ holds w.h.p. \paragraph*{Case I\hspace{-.1em}I\hspace{-.1em}I: $A^{(0)}\in\mathcal{B}_3$.} Suppose that $A^{(0)}\in \mathcal{B}_3$. From \cref{eqn:beta'bounds}, it holds w.h.p.~that  egin{align*} | eta'_z|&\geq |\lambda_z|| eta_z|-C\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty - C\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}} \ &\geq (1+\epsilon)| eta_z| + (\epsilon| eta_z|-C| eta_z|^2)+\left(\epsilon| eta_z|-C\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}}ight) \ &\geq (1+\epsilon)| eta_z|. \end{align*} Moreover, for any $j\in I_{<1}$, it holds w.h.p.~that  egin{align*} | eta'_j| \leq (1-3\epsilon)\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|_\infty + C\|{ oldsymbol  eta}\|^2_{\infty} + C\sqrt{ rac{\log n}{n}} \leq (1-\epsilon)| eta_z| \end{align*} These imply that $A^{(t+1)}
